1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:05,599
Daniel, a Master of Arts in Education student, signs in.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:12,100
Under Requests, Leave of Absence. The form shows the limits: two semesters at a time.

3
00:00:13,099 --> 00:00:18,300
Rules applied on this screen lists each rule with its Handbook page.

4
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:25,000
Daniel picks the dates, a reason, and a short explanation.

5
00:00:26,199 --> 00:00:29,699
A summary to check before sending.

6
00:00:29,899 --> 00:00:32,899
Submitted. The request waits for Graduate School staff.

7
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:35,199
Graduate School staff signs in.

8
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,699
The Leave of Absence board: stages are columns, requests are cards.

9
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:49,299
Graduate School staff drags the card to In staff review. The server checks every move.

10
00:00:55,700 --> 00:01:01,299
The policy check advises with Pass or Needs review. It never decides. The Dean does.

11
00:01:05,799 --> 00:01:10,799
Graduate School staff forwards the request to the Dean.

12
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,599
The card moves to With the Dean and locks for staff.

13
00:01:15,799 --> 00:01:18,099
The Dean signs in.

14
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:31,399
The Dean drags the card to Leave scheduled.

15
00:01:31,599 --> 00:01:35,700
Approved, flagged for the Registrar. The Dean could also deny it.

16
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:42,299
Graduate School staff signs in.

17
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:51,599
For the demo, Graduate School staff starts the leave by hand.

18
00:01:51,799 --> 00:01:54,799
Daniel is on leave, and enrollment is closed.

19
00:01:55,700 --> 00:02:00,200
The Registrar list. The portal sends no e-mail: staff sends it officially.

20
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:09,400
Graduate School staff marks the list sent to the Registrar.

21
00:02:10,099 --> 00:02:15,000
Daniel signs in again.

22
00:02:15,199 --> 00:02:18,300
The student's page shows the status On leave.
